-- Fix wording problems in public model descriptions (2026-11-04 catalogue audit).
--
-- Problems fixed here (254 rows; stale 88, truncated 73, marketing 45, competitor 31, typo 9, first_person 8):
-- * Stale status: "the latest", "most advanced", "This entry tracks a preview
--   release" on previews that have long been replaced or retired, and dates that
--   have passed.
-- * Marketing claims ("state-of-the-art", "SOTA", "industry-leading",
--   "world's best") and benchmark boasts.
-- * Names of aggregators and hosting providers ("listed by ...", "hosted by ...",
--   "exposed through ...") and first-person vendor copy.
-- * Text cut off mid-sentence with "...", scraped markdown, and typos
--   ("Noul" for yes/no).
-- Facts in the old text are kept; only the problem wording changes.

-- Guarded on the description observed during the 2026-11-04 audit: each row
-- carries the first 12 hex characters of md5(description) as it was then (null
-- for an empty description), so a row edited since is left alone. Row-level
-- history, including the previous text, is recorded by the catalogue_row_history
-- trigger on public.v2_models.
with fixes (model_slug, old_description_md5, new_description) as (
values
  ($d$ai21/jamba-large-1.7$d$::text, '9f7ca766238c'::text, $d$Jamba Large 1.7 is a model in AI21's Jamba open family, offering improvements in grounding, instruction-following, and overall efficiency. It supports up to 256K of input context for long documents, codebases, and agent workflows.$d$::text),
  ($d$aion-labs/aion-rp-llama-3.1-8b$d$::text, '1133e7538bf3'::text, $d$Aion-RP-Llama-3.1-8B is an AionLabs roleplaying and character-chat model fine-tuned from Meta's Llama 3.1 8B.$d$::text),
  ($d$alibaba/wan-2.6$d$::text, '212e2616c9a5'::text, $d$Wan 2.6 is Alibaba's video generation model, released in March 2026, supporting over 10 visual creation capabilities in a unified system. It generates 1080p video at 24fps from text, images, reference videos, or audio.$d$::text),
  ($d$alibaba/wan-2.7$d$::text, '421ab9d51a69'::text, $d$Wan 2.7 is a video generation model from Alibaba. It supports text-to-video, image-to-video with first and last frame control, and reference-to-video, where multiple reference images guide the style and content.$d$::text),
  ($d$amazon/nova-2-lite-v1$d$::text, '490ed8f1a6ea'::text, $d$Nova 2 Lite is a fast, cost-effective reasoning model for everyday workloads that can process text, images, and videos to generate text.$d$::text),
  ($d$amazon/nova-lite-v1$d$::text, '7a6f3ea4346c'::text, $d$Amazon Nova Lite 1.0 is a very low-cost multimodal model from Amazon that focuses on fast processing of image, video, and text inputs to generate text output.$d$::text),
  ($d$amazon/nova-micro-v1$d$::text, '43d4afa76b71'::text, $d$Amazon Nova Micro 1.0 is a text-only model that delivers the lowest latency responses in the Amazon Nova family of models at a very low cost.$d$::text),
  ($d$amazon/nova-premier-v1$d$::text, '0c095860f29b'::text, $d$Amazon Nova Premier is Amazon's Nova 1 multimodal model for complex reasoning tasks and for use as a teacher model when distilling custom models.$d$::text),
  ($d$amazon/nova-pro-v1$d$::text, '00caa27d3298'::text, $d$Amazon Nova Pro 1.0 is a capable multimodal model from Amazon focused on providing a combination of accuracy, speed, and cost for a wide range of tasks.$d$::text),
  ($d$anthropic/claude-3-haiku$d$::text, 'd4d5d7c5279d'::text, $d$Claude 3 Haiku was the fastest and most compact model in Anthropic's Claude 3 family, built for near-instant responsiveness. It accepts text and image inputs and produces text outputs.$d$::text),
  ($d$anthropic/claude-opus-4$d$::text, '3cd0de9f98e3'::text, $d$Claude Opus 4 was an Anthropic Opus-class model released in May 2025, built for sustained performance on complex, long-running tasks and agent workflows.$d$::text),
  ($d$anthropic/claude-opus-4.1$d$::text, 'c04513ee166f'::text, $d$Claude Opus 4.1 was an update to Claude Opus 4, with improved performance in coding, reasoning, and agentic tasks. It supports up to 200K of input context for long documents, codebases, and agent workflows.$d$::text),
  ($d$apodex/apodex-1.1-mini:free$d$::text, 'a660276013d2'::text, $d$Apodex 1.1 Mini is Apodex AI's open-weight, 35B-parameter reasoning model based on Qwen3.5-35B-A3B. It is designed for coding, research and tool-using agents, with a 262,144-token context window and an Apache 2.0 license.$d$::text),
  ($d$arcee-ai/virtuoso-large$d$::text, '38411e9f9902'::text, $d$Virtuoso-Large is Arcee's 72B-parameter general-purpose LLM, tuned for cross-domain reasoning, creative writing and enterprise QA.$d$::text),
  ($d$baichuan/baichuan-m2-32b$d$::text, 'a464b09a7c26'::text, $d$Baichuan-M2 32B is Baichuan's medically enhanced reasoning model for real-world medical reasoning tasks. It was trained with reinforcement learning against a large-scale verifier system while keeping its general capabilities.$d$::text),
  ($d$baidu/cobuddy$d$::text, '7c411159af19'::text, $d$CoBuddy is a code generation model from Baidu, optimized for coding and AI agent scenarios with high inference throughput and low end-to-end latency.$d$::text),
  ($d$baidu/ernie-4.5-0.3b$d$::text, '2321664b215b'::text, $d$ERNIE 4.5 0.3B is the smallest open-weight dense text model in Baidu's ERNIE 4.5 family.$d$::text),
  ($d$baidu/ernie-4.5-vl-28b-a3b$d$::text, '2723cc45f1ae'::text, $d$ERNIE 4.5 VL 28B A3B is a multimodal Mixture-of-Experts chat model from Baidu with 28B total parameters and 3B activated per token, built for text and vision understanding.$d$::text),
  ($d$baidu/paddleocr-vl-1.5$d$::text, '321c66c64c62'::text, $d$PaddleOCR-VL 1.5 is Baidu's vision-language model for document parsing, extracting text, tables, formulas and layout from document images.$d$::text),
  ($d$black-forest-labs/flux-1-kontext-max$d$::text, '451f7a13ff3e'::text, $d$FLUX.1 Kontext [max] is the highest-quality tier of Black Forest Labs' FLUX.1 Kontext models for in-context image generation and editing from text and reference images.$d$::text),
  ($d$black-forest-labs/flux-2-max$d$::text, 'aaf3339d76b5'::text, $d$FLUX.2 [max] is the highest-quality tier of Black Forest Labs' FLUX.2 image generation and editing models.$d$::text),
  ($d$black-forest-labs/flux-video-upscale$d$::text, '1bcca29d2af0'::text, $d$FLUX Video Upscale is a video upscaling model from Black Forest Labs. It enlarges a single source video by 1.5× to 3× while preserving its duration.$d$::text),
  ($d$bytedance-seed/seed-1.6-flash$d$::text, '0dac59548f64'::text, $d$Seed 1.6 Flash is an ultra-fast multimodal deep thinking model by ByteDance Seed, supporting both text and visual understanding. It features a 256K context window.$d$::text),
  ($d$bytedance-seed/seed-2-1-turbo$d$::text, '6ad0ce0fffe3'::text, $d$Seed 2.1 Turbo is a multimodal model from ByteDance Seed for coding and long-horizon agent workflows. It is suited for end-to-end software delivery, multi-step task execution, and visual understanding.$d$::text),
  ($d$bytedance-seed/seed-2.0-code$d$::text, 'f78fa32337d4'::text, $d$Seed 2.0 Code is a model from ByteDance Seed optimized for agentic coding. It is suited for frontend development, multilingual programming tasks, and coding-agent workflows.$d$::text),
  ($d$bytedance-seed/seed-2.0-lite$d$::text, '0cf29e12c40c'::text, $d$Seed 2.0 Lite is a cost-efficient general-purpose model from ByteDance Seed with multimodal and agent capabilities and lower latency, suited as a default choice for most production workloads.$d$::text),
  ($d$bytedance-seed/seed-2.0-mini$d$::text, '312a88f08ac3'::text, $d$Seed 2.0 Mini is a ByteDance Seed model for latency-sensitive, high-concurrency, and cost-sensitive workloads. It supports a 256K context window, four reasoning effort modes (minimal, low, medium, high), and multimodal understanding.$d$::text),
  ($d$bytedance/seedance-2.0-mini$d$::text, '5d7faba1fc74'::text, $d$Seedance 2.0 Mini is a video generation model from ByteDance. It supports text-to-video, image-to-video with first and last frame control, and multimodal reference-to-video with image, video, and audio inputs.$d$::text),
  ($d$bytedance/ui-tars-1.5-7b$d$::text, 'b7603fe69fcb'::text, $d$UI-TARS-1.5 is a multimodal vision-language agent from ByteDance, optimized for GUI-based environments including desktop interfaces, web browsers, mobile systems, and games.$d$::text),
  ($d$cloudflare/clef$d$::text, 'a14179476bc6'::text, $d$Clef is a Cloudflare 27B multimodal model for typed yes/no, choice, and score decisions.$d$::text),
  ($d$cloudflare/clef-flash$d$::text, 'a3f93932ff6d'::text, $d$Clef Flash is a Cloudflare 9B multimodal model for typed yes/no, choice, and score decisions.$d$::text),
  ($d$cognitivecomputations/dolphin-mistral-24b-venice-edition$d$::text, '5c5eb8cd18d5'::text, $d$Dolphin Mistral 24B Venice Edition is a fine-tuned variant of Mistral-Small-24B-Instruct-2501, developed by dphn.ai in collaboration with Venice.ai as an uncensored instruct-tuned LLM.$d$::text),
  ($d$cohere/command-r-08-2024$d$::text, 'a618dd15e8df'::text, $d$Command R (08-2024) is the August 2024 update of Cohere's Command R, with improved multilingual retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), tool use, math, code and reasoning.$d$::text),
  ($d$cohere/command-r-plus-08-2024$d$::text, '153908bc2dbc'::text, $d$Command R+ (08-2024) is the August 2024 update of Cohere's Command R+, with roughly 50% higher throughput and 25% lower latency than the previous version on the same hardware footprint.$d$::text),
  ($d$cohere/command-r7b-12-2024$d$::text, '3273e32ec1c9'::text, $d$Command R7B (12-2024) is the smallest model in Cohere's Command R family, released in December 2024 for retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), tool use and agent tasks.$d$::text),
  ($d$cohere/north-mini-code$d$::text, 'bcfe98cea871'::text, $d$North Mini Code is Cohere's first agentic coding model and the debut of its North family. It is a sparse mixture-of-experts model with 30B total parameters and 3B active.$d$::text),
  ($d$deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3-0324$d$::text, '44835f5ee4ba'::text, $d$DeepSeek V3 (0324) is the March 2025 update of DeepSeek's V3 chat model, a 685B-parameter mixture-of-experts model. It succeeds the original [DeepSeek V3](/deepseek/deepseek-v3).$d$::text),
  ($d$deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3.1$d$::text, '560ea8de1980'::text, $d$DeepSeek-V3.1 is a large hybrid reasoning model (671B parameters, 37B active) that supports both thinking and non-thinking modes via prompt templates.$d$::text),
  ($d$deepseek/deepseek-r1$d$::text, '3878d0bade0f'::text, $d$DeepSeek R1 is DeepSeek's open-weight reasoning model, released in January 2025 with fully open reasoning tokens. It has 671B total parameters with 37B active per token.$d$::text),
  ($d$deepseek/deepseek-r1-0528$d$::text, 'd7e30c397ba2'::text, $d$DeepSeek R1 0528 is the May 28, 2025 update to the [original DeepSeek R1](/deepseek/deepseek-r1), an open-weight reasoning model with 671B total parameters, 37B active per token, and fully open reasoning tokens.$d$::text),
  ($d$deepseek/deepseek-r1-2025-01-20$d$::text, 'b1565756a2d7'::text, $d$DeepSeek R1 (2025-01-20) is the original January 2025 release of DeepSeek's open-weight reasoning model, with fully open reasoning tokens.$d$::text),
  ($d$deepseek/deepseek-r1-2025-05-28$d$::text, '6d00ac62a794'::text, $d$DeepSeek R1 (2025-05-28) is the May 2025 update to DeepSeek's open-weight R1 reasoning model, with fully open reasoning tokens.$d$::text),
  ($d$deepseek/deepseek-r1-distill-llama-70b$d$::text, 'ffd28d006d8c'::text, $d$DeepSeek R1 Distill Llama 70B is a reasoning model distilled from DeepSeek R1 into Meta's Llama 3.3 70B.$d$::text),
  ($d$deepseek/deepseek-r1-distill-qwen-32b$d$::text, '575233761568'::text, $d$DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B is a reasoning model distilled from DeepSeek-R1 into Qwen2.5 32B. DeepSeek reports it outperforms OpenAI o1-mini across various benchmarks.$d$::text),
  ($d$deepseek/deepseek-v3-0324$d$::text, '44835f5ee4ba'::text, $d$DeepSeek V3 (0324) is the March 2025 update of DeepSeek's V3 chat model, a 685B-parameter mixture-of-experts model. It succeeds the original [DeepSeek V3](/deepseek/deepseek-v3).$d$::text),
  ($d$deepseek/deepseek-v3.1-terminus$d$::text, '253472f7fb7f'::text, $d$DeepSeek V3.1 Terminus is an update to [DeepSeek V3.1](/deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3.1) that keeps the model's original capabilities while addressing user-reported issues, including language consistency and agent capabilities.$d$::text),
  ($d$deepseek/deepseek-v3.2-exp$d$::text, '6af8a2f36c24'::text, $d$DeepSeek V3.2 Exp is an experimental model DeepSeek released in September 2025 as an intermediate step between V3.1 and V3.2, introducing DeepSeek Sparse Attention.$d$::text),
  ($d$deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813$d$::text, '08adf1550691'::text, $d$DeepSeek V4 Pro 0813 is the 13 August 2026 version served by DeepSeek's stable deepseek-v4-pro API slug. It supports thinking and non-thinking modes, JSON output, tool calls, Chat Completions, Responses, Anthropic Messages, prefix completion, fill-in-the-middle completion, a 1M-token context window, and up to 384K output tokens.$d$::text),
  ($d$dots-studio/dots-3-note-preview$d$::text, 'bb1fe1866fe8'::text, $d$Dots3-Note Preview is an open-weight mixture-of-experts model from Dots Studio, with 16B active parameters out of 280B total. It is the lightest model in the Dots 3 family.$d$::text),
  ($d$early-access/ea-29b-a4b$d$::text, '74124c220568'::text, $d$ea-29b-a4b is an open-weight text model offered in early access.$d$::text),
  ($d$google/gemini-1.5-flash-002$d$::text, '3ae9c079821b'::text, $d$Gemini 1.5 Flash 002 was the September 2024 update of Gemini 1.5 Flash, Google's fast multimodal model for low-latency, high-volume workloads, with text, image, video and audio input.$d$::text),
  ($d$google/gemini-1.5-flash-8b$d$::text, '8e2712c816e1'::text, $d$Gemini 1.5 Flash 8B was the smallest Gemini 1.5 model, an 8B-parameter variant of Gemini 1.5 Flash for low-cost, high-volume multimodal tasks.$d$::text),
  ($d$google/gemini-2.0-flash-thinking-exp-2024-12-19$d$::text, '020b618a2354'::text, $d$Gemini 2.0 Flash Thinking Exp (2024-12-19) was an experimental Gemini 2.0 Flash reasoning model from Google that showed its thinking process.$d$::text),
  ($d$google/gemini-2.0-flash-thinking-exp-2025-01-21$d$::text, 'f1404e19981c'::text, $d$Gemini 2.0 Flash Thinking Exp (2025-01-21) was an experimental Gemini 2.0 Flash reasoning model from Google that showed its thinking process.$d$::text),
  ($d$google/gemini-2.5-flash-image$d$::text, '963e87a9f500'::text, $d$Gemini 2.5 Flash Image (Nano Banana) was Google's generally available image generation and editing model with contextual understanding, released in October 2025. It supports text and image inputs for generation, restyling, or edit-style workflows.$d$::text),
  ($d$google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite-preview-2025-06-17$d$::text, 'cb6999a72294'::text, $d$Gemini 2.5 Flash Lite Preview (2025-06-17) was the preview release of Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite, Google's high-efficiency multimodal model for low-latency, high-volume workloads.$d$::text),
  ($d$google/gemini-2.5-flash-preview-2025-05-20$d$::text, '7ffff26989d4'::text, $d$Gemini 2.5 Flash Preview (2025-05-20) was a preview update of Gemini 2.5 Flash, Google's hybrid reasoning model for fast, high-volume multimodal workloads.$d$::text),
